    "updated_at": "2021-09-16T16:54:51Z",
    "body": "One quick addendum: if user agents implement service worker partitioning ([ref](https://github.com/privacycg/storage-partitioning)) then the cookie's partition key should be the site of the worker's partition key.\r\n\r\nIf user agents don't implement storage partitioning, then partitioned cookies may need to be blocked in service workers. Otherwise, service workers could use partitioned cookies as a cross-site identifier. See [the CHIPS explainer](https://github.com/WICG/CHIPS#service-workers) for more detail.\r\n\r\nService worker partitioning is also mentioned in more detail in [this proposal](https://github.com/wanderview/quota-storage-partitioning/blob/main/explainer.md#serviceworker-api).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
